    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nCurrently, the way to quit a hover window displayed by for example LSP `K` is either to\n- press `K` again to focus the hover window then press `q`, or\n- move the cursor.\n\nPressing `<esc>` when focus is on the hover window has no effect, and pressing `<c-c>` shows `Type  :qa  and press <Enter> to exit Nvim`.\n\nRelated: https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/27288\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nI suggest the following when `<c-c>` or `<esc>` is pressed:\n- If the hover window's buffer is modifiable, show `Press  q  to exit this hover window, or  :fclose!  to close all floating windows` on the command-line.\n- Otherwise, just close it.\n\nThe modifiable case is mostly a corner case (\"some plugins\"), suggested by https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/27288#issuecomment-2336691578 . If we don't care about that case, a simpler solution is to close it either way.",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I think this would fall under the role of `<Plug>(nvim-closewin)`  https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/31706 , and adds another use-case to it.",
